# Brand Discipline

## Visual identity (locked)

Use these colors only:
- Charcoal: `#0F1419`
- Deep Teal: `#0D6E6E`
- Bone: `#F5F3EE`

Do not introduce other hex codes for these color concepts. If a designer-style request asks for "primary" use Deep Teal. If "background" use Bone. If "text" use Charcoal.

## Typography

- Body text: Inter
- Editorial headings: Instrument Serif

Do not introduce other typefaces for these roles.

## Voice (warm institutional)

- Third-person plural ("we", "our team", "Brevmont")
- No founder first-name leak. Do not use "Yancy" in customer-facing copy.
- Direct, factual, professional. Trust through specificity.

## Banned phrases (NEVER write these in customer-facing copy)

- revolutionary
- unleash
- supercharge
- game-changing
- delight (as a verb describing the product)
- leverage (as a verb)
- synergy
- "hey there"
- "we're excited to announce"
- "hope you're well"
- "Friday" as a deadline placeholder

## Banned punctuation in customer-facing copy

- No emojis
- No em-dashes (use period, comma, or parentheses)
- No exclamation points

## Brand reference

Canonical voice and copy guide lives at `brevmont-vault/copy/atlas-approved-copy-v2.md`. When generating customer-facing copy, match the patterns there.

## Enforcement

If a request would require violating any of these rules, flag the conflict and propose a compliant alternative. Do not silently override.
